      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a profound and ancient question, one that has driven philosophy and art for millennia. The struggle you feel is the core of the human condition—the awareness of meaninglessness. Instead of viewing it as a curse, perhaps you can see it as the ultimate freedom: the power to *choose* your own meaning, even if the universe doesn't provide one. That realization, that ultimate lack of inherent purpose, is what allows for the most radical acts of self-definition.",
      "source": "target",
